WEBVTT

00:11.011 --> 00:15.015
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

00:20.311 --> 00:22.313
Here.

00:27.318 --> 00:29.779
Hurry! That woman is… How awful.

00:34.117 --> 00:35.618
Mr. Heo, let's go.

00:37.162 --> 00:40.081
You know it'd be bad
if Mr. Kim saw me here.

01:09.986 --> 01:11.029
I'm sorry.

01:12.989 --> 01:14.032
I never imagined…

01:15.992 --> 01:17.118
I just wanted

01:17.786 --> 01:20.914
to prove to you what I saw.

01:28.171 --> 01:29.506
Please drop me off here.

01:30.340 --> 01:31.925
I'll walk the rest.

01:44.479 --> 01:46.272
Thank you for the ride.

01:47.315 --> 01:48.650
See you in tomorrow's class.

01:56.950 --> 02:00.078
Tell me the truth,
and don't you dare think about lying.

02:02.288 --> 02:05.542
Did you really not know,
or did you just pretend not to?

02:06.626 --> 02:07.460
Sorry?

02:08.253 --> 02:09.129
What do you mean?

02:09.629 --> 02:12.298
Why didn't you tell me
who Se-yun's dad is?

02:13.800 --> 02:15.593
Don't tell me you didn't know.

02:18.221 --> 02:19.347
What do you…

02:20.098 --> 02:21.391
Who is Mr. Kim?

02:23.977 --> 02:25.562
Don't know Kim Su-hun, the author?

03:00.763 --> 03:02.307
Kim Su-hun, the author?

03:03.892 --> 03:05.393
Kim Su-hun, the author…

03:07.187 --> 03:09.355
So Se-yun's dad is an author.

03:09.439 --> 03:10.607
No wonder.

03:12.358 --> 03:14.694
I'm not too familiar with many authors.

03:17.197 --> 03:18.281
So what?

03:19.365 --> 03:20.992
So what if he's Kim Su-hun?

03:22.535 --> 03:24.120
Is that important right now?

04:01.032 --> 04:03.952
So it was you all along, Kim Su-hun.

04:24.264 --> 04:25.473
Mom.

04:39.779 --> 04:42.240
Right, it's you.

05:05.847 --> 05:06.931
Mun-oh?

05:08.391 --> 05:10.560
You skipped class too?

05:22.447 --> 05:23.281
Oh, here.

05:24.907 --> 05:25.950
What's this?

05:28.161 --> 05:31.247
I adore this poet. How did you know?

05:32.081 --> 05:33.624
Oh my gosh.

05:36.544 --> 05:38.963
Thank you so much for this, Mun-oh.

05:39.047 --> 05:41.090
I'll see you later.

05:44.218 --> 05:46.054
-Eun-joo.
-Su-hun!

05:46.804 --> 05:47.764
Well, well.

05:48.806 --> 05:50.975
What a surprise. Where are you headed?

06:03.696 --> 06:05.615
Please don't think too much.

06:06.657 --> 06:09.660
The most important thing to me
is that you feel at peace.

06:10.370 --> 06:13.081
In our family,
nothing matters more than that.

07:13.891 --> 07:15.852
Kim Su-hun, you son of a bitch.

07:18.187 --> 07:20.189
How could you betray dear Eun-joo…

07:37.039 --> 07:43.379
We don't call everything that happens
in our daily lives an incident, do we?

07:43.463 --> 07:44.964
Regardless of size,

07:45.590 --> 07:48.551
if an event has a significant impact

07:49.552 --> 07:52.388
on the lives and actions
of the characters,

07:53.181 --> 07:57.268
then we can call it a narrative incident.

08:00.271 --> 08:02.440
And such events…

08:09.780 --> 08:10.907
always stem from…

08:13.576 --> 08:15.328
the intricate conflicts

08:16.370 --> 08:17.497
within the human mind…

08:26.088 --> 08:27.006
I'm sorry.

08:27.757 --> 08:29.258
So these conflicts…

08:30.218 --> 08:32.345
Hold on. Where was I?

08:42.647 --> 08:44.065
My office, now.

08:54.033 --> 08:55.409
You punk.

08:57.328 --> 08:59.455
Why do you always sit

09:00.081 --> 09:02.833
in the last row of the lecture hall?

09:04.210 --> 09:05.545
It's so you can daydream

09:06.921 --> 09:08.965
instead of paying attention, isn't it?

09:11.300 --> 09:13.302
You can see everything from there.

09:14.845 --> 09:18.599
A seat where I can observe everything
without being seen myself.

09:25.147 --> 09:25.982
Listen.

09:29.193 --> 09:30.778
About what happened last night.

09:31.779 --> 09:33.114
Tell me more about it.

09:33.990 --> 09:36.409
What was her name again? Min-hui?

09:36.492 --> 09:40.246
Seon Min-hui, was it?
The woman who got into that accident.

09:41.330 --> 09:42.415
And

09:43.374 --> 09:44.208
Kim Su…

09:45.334 --> 09:46.586
Se-yun's dad.

09:48.129 --> 09:49.755
What's he been doing since then?

09:51.007 --> 09:51.841
Tell me.

09:55.136 --> 09:55.970
What?

09:58.556 --> 09:59.473
You don't want to?

10:02.935 --> 10:05.605
You should at least tell me.

10:06.188 --> 10:09.358
I was also there last night,
thanks to you.

10:09.442 --> 10:10.401
She's dead.

10:16.198 --> 10:17.241
Dead?

10:18.284 --> 10:19.327
The police called

10:19.952 --> 10:21.370
this morning.

10:31.839 --> 10:32.923
So, in the end…

10:37.261 --> 10:38.179
In the end…

10:40.056 --> 10:41.140
So, in the end…

10:45.269 --> 10:47.772
Mr. Heo, do you know
Kim Su-hun personally?

10:48.272 --> 10:49.565
How well do you know him?

10:53.194 --> 10:54.028
What?

10:55.363 --> 10:56.739
I don't know him that well.

10:57.490 --> 11:00.534
I just know he's a famous author,
that's all.

11:01.035 --> 11:02.411
Why are you lying?

11:06.123 --> 11:06.957
What did you say?

11:08.959 --> 11:10.711
I heard you two are friends.

11:11.212 --> 11:15.132
Se-yun told me
that you hosted the special lecture

11:15.716 --> 11:17.051
he gave at school recently.

11:19.095 --> 11:19.929
Look.

11:20.846 --> 11:24.058
Do you think only friends
can host a discussion?

11:25.476 --> 11:27.228
We just went to college together.

11:29.980 --> 11:32.191
I don't know him that well. Wait.

11:33.693 --> 11:34.694
Why do you ask?

11:36.946 --> 11:38.072
Well, Mr. Kim…

11:44.161 --> 11:45.287
What about Kim Su-hun?

11:48.541 --> 11:50.376
I just wonder what kind of person he is.

11:51.252 --> 11:53.629
I liked him at first,
but now he seems strange.

11:54.714 --> 11:57.758
He's way too calm,
considering what happened last night.

11:58.467 --> 12:01.512
That's not the only strange thing.
I wrote it down here, so…

12:05.224 --> 12:06.934
-You wrote it already?
-Oh, but…

12:10.312 --> 12:11.522
It's my last assignment.

12:13.983 --> 12:15.443
You said so yesterday.

12:16.318 --> 12:17.903
That our lessons are over now.

12:18.738 --> 12:20.239
And now, with what happened…

12:28.289 --> 12:29.999
I have my convenience store gig now.

12:35.796 --> 12:37.298
Thank you,

12:38.758 --> 12:40.509
and sorry about everything, Mr. Heo.

12:41.010 --> 12:42.136
That's not…

12:44.513 --> 12:45.806
Hey, I…

13:17.421 --> 13:20.633
When the line between beauty
and ugliness gets blurred,

13:21.133 --> 13:23.677
everything becomes a question mark.

13:26.180 --> 13:29.141
That's what the world was like
this morning.

13:29.225 --> 13:31.393
She didn't come to work yesterday either?

13:33.479 --> 13:34.772
And without notice?

13:37.399 --> 13:39.026
Oh my, I had no idea.

13:39.652 --> 13:42.363
I called her
at least three times yesterday,

13:42.446 --> 13:43.948
but she didn't pick up.

13:45.115 --> 13:48.118
She's just being petty
because I gave her a stern talking-to.

13:48.619 --> 13:50.162
What an awful attitude.

13:50.663 --> 13:53.082
After I went out of my way
to talk to her that day.

13:53.999 --> 13:58.003
I think generosity and compassion
are wasted on people like her.

13:59.046 --> 14:01.006
I'm not letting this slide anymore.

14:01.090 --> 14:02.633
Yeah, let her quit.

14:03.717 --> 14:07.388
Didn't I tell you before
not to stress yourself out over her?

14:07.888 --> 14:09.849
I'll tell her when she comes tomorrow.

14:10.349 --> 14:13.769
You don't think
she'll be a no-show tomorrow too, do you?

14:15.479 --> 14:16.313
What you doing?

14:17.523 --> 14:18.899
It's nothing.

14:22.987 --> 14:24.989
Hey. Are you all ready to go?

14:26.031 --> 14:29.034
Just wait a bit.
I'm almost done setting the table.

14:30.244 --> 14:34.248
No complaining about side dishes today.
Especially you, Kim Se-yun.

14:34.331 --> 14:36.417
Just say "it's good," and eat.

14:37.710 --> 14:38.836
What's going on?

14:38.919 --> 14:40.671
Don't worry about it.

14:42.047 --> 14:44.717
I'll be making the side dishes
for the time being.

14:46.510 --> 14:49.346
Or we can buy them
until we hire someone new.

14:50.097 --> 14:52.308
Wait, Min-hui's quitting?

14:52.808 --> 14:54.268
Why? When did she quit?

14:54.351 --> 14:57.062
She must be sulking.
Your mom told her off.

14:57.146 --> 14:59.106
She's gone radio silent since yesterday.

15:01.609 --> 15:04.361
Why, honey?
Are you sad to hear she's quitting?

15:05.571 --> 15:08.032
No, it's not like that.
Don't worry about it.

15:11.327 --> 15:14.955
No, Kang. You should just eat up.
You'll be late for school.

15:17.374 --> 15:18.208
Kang, sit.

15:22.588 --> 15:24.173
Yes, hello?

15:25.424 --> 15:26.258
Excuse me?

15:28.260 --> 15:29.094
The police?

15:32.973 --> 15:33.807
What?

15:35.225 --> 15:36.685
What do you mean…

15:44.652 --> 15:45.903
Oh my God.

15:49.031 --> 15:51.533
-Honey, this is terrible.
-What's going on?

15:53.118 --> 15:53.953
Honey.

15:54.578 --> 15:57.665
It's Min-hui. Yesterday, she… I mean,

15:58.290 --> 15:59.625
early this morning…

16:00.125 --> 16:01.126
Min-hui?

16:01.210 --> 16:02.336
What about her?

16:04.713 --> 16:05.673
Hello?

16:06.173 --> 16:07.549
Yes, what's this about?

16:08.759 --> 16:10.511
Yes, you can tell me.

16:17.518 --> 16:18.686
What is it, Mrs. Ahn?

16:19.520 --> 16:21.063
What about Min-hui…

16:24.441 --> 16:26.151
She died in a car accident?

16:26.694 --> 16:27.820
In the ER?

16:31.615 --> 16:33.784
What do you mean "no family"?
That's impossible.

16:36.245 --> 16:37.329
Well, honestly,

16:37.413 --> 16:39.915
we don't really know much
about her family either…

16:43.377 --> 16:45.212
Yun! What…

16:45.295 --> 16:46.338
What's wrong?

16:46.422 --> 16:48.090
-Yes, let me know.
-What's wrong?

16:48.173 --> 16:50.426
-Yes.
-What's wrong?

16:50.926 --> 16:53.637
-Not the home phone. Call my cell.
-Yun, what's wrong?

16:53.721 --> 16:55.764
-Yun.
-My cell phone number is…

16:55.848 --> 16:58.183
-Easy. Can you lift his head?
-My number's 010…

16:59.435 --> 17:01.937
-248, then 5117.
-Yun?

17:02.021 --> 17:03.105
-Yes, thanks.
-Yun?

17:03.689 --> 17:07.609
Focus on my voice.
Yun, just keep breathing, will you?

17:12.823 --> 17:15.784
Do what we learned at the hospital.
Breathe. There you go.

17:16.368 --> 17:17.703
Keep rubbing his hand.

17:32.092 --> 17:33.510
Do you think he'll be okay?

17:34.178 --> 17:36.263
Maybe we should get him to a doctor?

17:36.346 --> 17:39.850
He's just in shock.
There's no need to see a doctor for that.

17:40.350 --> 17:44.063
He took a sedative,
so he'll be fine after he sleeps it off.

17:45.355 --> 17:47.524
Let's go. We should let him sleep.

17:55.032 --> 17:57.785
His problem is that he's too weak-hearted.

17:59.286 --> 18:02.956
I thought playing sports would help,
but he hasn't changed a bit.

18:03.457 --> 18:04.750
Are you okay?

18:07.252 --> 18:08.462
No.

18:08.962 --> 18:10.881
If I'm honest, I'm heartbroken too.

18:12.424 --> 18:15.427
I can't stop thinking about
how mean I was to Min-hui.

18:18.472 --> 18:20.307
That day, I shouldn't have let her

18:20.933 --> 18:22.643
walk away like that.

18:27.731 --> 18:30.526
You're overthinking again.

18:31.110 --> 18:33.153
You didn't do anything wrong.

18:34.738 --> 18:35.906
It's okay.

18:36.949 --> 18:39.451
Our lives are in the hands of fate.
It's a shame, but…

18:39.535 --> 18:43.455
When the line between kindness
and cruelty gets blurred,

18:44.540 --> 18:46.458
everything becomes a question mark.

18:59.471 --> 19:03.517
Like that smile that harbors
some unknown malice.

19:16.113 --> 19:17.156
"Malice"?

19:20.284 --> 19:21.201
Malice.

19:27.833 --> 19:28.834
Malice…

19:32.004 --> 19:34.006
Malice? What does he mean by that?

19:45.976 --> 19:47.019
Have a good one.

20:05.704 --> 20:06.538
Welcome…

20:08.582 --> 20:09.541
Mr. Heo?

20:15.380 --> 20:17.299
A pack of these.

20:19.509 --> 20:21.094
How did you know I worked here?

20:21.845 --> 20:25.390
You told me that you worked at
the convenience store by the intersection.

20:28.977 --> 20:30.395
Did you come here to see me?

20:30.479 --> 20:32.731
I was on my way home
and out of cigarettes.

20:35.776 --> 20:37.152
Why are you grinning?

20:37.236 --> 20:38.070
They're obvious.

20:39.279 --> 20:40.155
Your lies.

20:43.283 --> 20:44.618
What do you want to say?

20:46.203 --> 20:47.246
That's why you're here.

20:50.123 --> 20:52.334
If you're not too busy, let's talk.

20:58.048 --> 20:59.174
You know…

21:01.343 --> 21:04.846
I only said we should stop our lessons…

21:07.641 --> 21:10.894
because I got mad.

21:14.898 --> 21:15.857
What about you?

21:16.858 --> 21:19.945
Don't you think you'd regret it
if we just end them like this?

21:23.448 --> 21:24.408
I would

21:25.117 --> 21:26.660
love to continue, of course.

21:27.661 --> 21:29.204
And I want to keep writing.

21:32.416 --> 21:34.251
I just wonder if you'd be all right.

21:34.334 --> 21:35.168
About Mr. Kim…

21:37.004 --> 21:40.215
Since you know him personally,
this must be awkward.

21:42.050 --> 21:43.051
That's true.

21:45.595 --> 21:48.432
Ethically speaking,
I am conflicted about it.

21:49.933 --> 21:51.601
Even if we're not close,

21:52.853 --> 21:55.355
he's not a complete stranger either.

21:56.606 --> 21:59.651
But, for the sake of your studies,

22:00.152 --> 22:02.696
I think it'd only be my duty as a teacher

22:03.405 --> 22:06.658
to continue the lessons
as originally planned.

22:08.160 --> 22:09.161
Besides,

22:10.787 --> 22:12.247
I think it's only right…

22:14.708 --> 22:16.418
for me to be braver

22:16.918 --> 22:18.086
at times like these.

22:20.839 --> 22:22.841
As long as you're okay with it…

22:26.636 --> 22:27.679
Thank you.

22:28.180 --> 22:29.723
Thank you.

22:29.806 --> 22:31.308
Frankly speaking,

22:31.391 --> 22:34.353
it doesn't really matter to me
who Mr. Kim is.

22:35.729 --> 22:38.440
What I'm learning from you
is far more important.

22:42.944 --> 22:44.988
Now that's what I like to hear.

22:45.489 --> 22:47.032
That's the attitude.

22:49.993 --> 22:52.454
We just need to continue our lessons

22:53.080 --> 22:54.998
with that very mindset, okay?

23:00.045 --> 23:01.171
But

23:01.922 --> 23:03.131
there's no need

23:03.715 --> 23:06.301
to tell Kim Su-hun about me.

23:07.677 --> 23:08.845
You understand, right?

23:09.346 --> 23:12.099
The minute you do,
you can say goodbye to our lessons.

23:12.182 --> 23:13.433
I know, Mr. Heo.

23:13.517 --> 23:14.893
I know that much.

23:15.894 --> 23:17.521
I don't want to tell him either.

23:18.021 --> 23:20.023
I don't even want to talk
to Mr. Kim anymore.

23:20.107 --> 23:21.400
You've read what I wrote.

23:35.914 --> 23:39.459
Speaking of your assignment,

23:39.960 --> 23:42.254
what did you mean by that last bit?

23:42.337 --> 23:43.171
"Malice"?

23:45.215 --> 23:46.049
How would I know?

23:47.676 --> 23:50.053
I just wrote what I saw and felt
in the moment.

23:52.055 --> 23:55.892
Like I told you before,
you're too quick to jump to conclusions.

23:55.976 --> 23:59.479
If you're going to use a word like that,
you have to have a reason.

23:59.563 --> 24:00.397
Reason?

24:00.981 --> 24:03.108
You said those two were dating.

24:03.191 --> 24:07.112
Yet he smiled to himself
when his lover died? It doesn't add up.

24:07.195 --> 24:08.947
Are you doubting me again?

24:09.448 --> 24:10.657
I saw it as clear as day!

24:10.740 --> 24:13.118
No, I'm not doubting you.

24:14.035 --> 24:18.331
The character and plot lack
the plausibility to call it malice.

24:18.999 --> 24:21.042
First, we need to find out

24:21.126 --> 24:23.920
what happened between them
right before the accident.

24:25.380 --> 24:26.381
So,

24:27.674 --> 24:29.009
are you asking me

24:29.968 --> 24:31.052
to go to that hotel?

24:32.971 --> 24:34.097
Now you're getting it.

24:36.099 --> 24:37.434
Put differently…

24:39.936 --> 24:40.812
this is

24:41.813 --> 24:43.231
an investigative assignment.

24:44.733 --> 24:47.152
By investigating,
we'll bring realism to your story.

24:51.406 --> 24:53.366
Do you know my heart just skipped a beat?

24:53.867 --> 24:54.826
So you're telling me

24:55.327 --> 24:59.080
to go there in person
and dig into the scene, right?

25:00.248 --> 25:02.792
-Don't get so worked up. Sit.
-Yes, sir.

25:03.293 --> 25:04.794
Why are you getting so worked up?

25:04.878 --> 25:07.380
Best to stay calm,
especially in situations like this.

25:08.173 --> 25:10.842
Okay. I have some time tomorrow afternoon.

25:10.926 --> 25:12.010
All right, then.

25:12.719 --> 25:13.678
I'll be going.

25:15.722 --> 25:17.349
Would you like to come with me?

25:18.558 --> 25:19.392
Me?

25:21.019 --> 25:22.437
Why would I go there?

25:22.521 --> 25:23.563
Why not?

25:24.439 --> 25:25.815
Are you scared of losing face?

25:27.567 --> 25:30.445
Face? Please.
I have important plans tomorrow.

25:32.822 --> 25:35.158
You punk, do you think I'm lying?

25:38.787 --> 25:40.288
What are you doing tomorrow?

25:47.128 --> 25:48.463
If you aren't busy…

25:50.590 --> 25:54.344
I was thinking we could go out.
Watch a movie or something.

26:00.934 --> 26:02.852
Can't you tell?

26:03.687 --> 26:04.729
I'm…

26:06.815 --> 26:08.608
asking you out on a date.

26:48.148 --> 26:49.733
Damn it, my car keys.

26:50.317 --> 26:51.192
My car keys.

26:51.860 --> 26:53.612
They're not here? Where are they?

26:53.695 --> 26:56.656
My darn car keys!

27:09.002 --> 27:11.796
Mr. Heo, I just got back from the hotel.

27:11.880 --> 27:15.759
If I start on my assignment now,
it should be in your inbox in two hours.

27:15.842 --> 27:17.886
There are so many shocking developments.

27:22.849 --> 27:24.434
He asked you out on a date?

27:25.852 --> 27:27.520
Yesterday, out of the blue.

27:28.313 --> 27:31.358
He asked to go to the movies alone,
but that would be no fun.

27:32.025 --> 27:33.610
So I asked you to join us.

27:35.820 --> 27:38.281
Or maybe you invited us
to brag about your date.

27:38.365 --> 27:39.741
Brag? Oh, please.

27:42.369 --> 27:43.787
You're so cheeky.

27:44.287 --> 27:46.373
Can't you just turn a blind eye for once?

27:46.456 --> 27:49.584
You're not the only couple
that goes on dates.

27:49.668 --> 27:50.919
Right, honey?

27:56.383 --> 27:58.176
What are you doing? Answer me.

27:59.344 --> 28:00.345
Answer what?

28:04.849 --> 28:05.975
He's been weird lately…

28:06.059 --> 28:08.103
It's been two hours.
Where's your assignment?

28:09.104 --> 28:11.106
He's acting out of character? How?

28:12.982 --> 28:14.734
He sleeps in my room sometimes.

28:16.236 --> 28:17.070
Oh my!

28:17.654 --> 28:21.157
Wow, Mun-oh. That's great! Wow.

28:25.036 --> 28:26.621
No, this is a good thing.

28:26.705 --> 28:30.500
That explains why you've been glowing
these days, Hyeon-suk.

28:30.583 --> 28:31.418
Excuse me?

28:32.043 --> 28:34.546
What are you talking about? I always glow.

28:34.629 --> 28:37.090
-You have always been beautiful.
-Yeah.

28:37.590 --> 28:38.633
Mun-oh.

28:39.134 --> 28:43.680
Please, just be good to Hyeon-suk.
Don't leave her lonely like back then.

28:44.180 --> 28:45.807
Hey, back then?

28:46.307 --> 28:47.434
Yeah, in the past.

28:48.226 --> 28:50.603
When you had multiple miscarriages.

28:51.104 --> 28:52.814
And when you were trying IVF.

28:54.315 --> 28:56.735
Why are you bringing that up right now?

28:56.818 --> 28:58.695
Mun-oh was so inattentive then.

29:00.280 --> 29:01.823
Do you even know

29:01.906 --> 29:04.576
how lonely she was
and how much she suffered back then?

29:04.659 --> 29:06.953
Come on, honey. What's with you?

29:07.036 --> 29:08.663
What, am I wrong?

29:09.748 --> 29:11.207
That's how you were.

29:11.833 --> 29:12.834
You were exhausted…

29:12.917 --> 29:16.087
I just sent you my assignment.
Sorry for the delay, Mr. Heo.

29:16.171 --> 29:20.133
…yet you were more worried about Mun-oh's
creative slump or whatever than yourself.

29:20.759 --> 29:22.510
I'm going to go to the restroom.

29:22.594 --> 29:24.220
Yes, go ahead.

29:29.058 --> 29:30.769
I hate to tell you "I told you so,"

29:31.269 --> 29:34.147
but you were so head over heels
for a writer.

29:34.230 --> 29:35.064
Hey!

29:35.148 --> 29:39.277
He left because he's embarrassed.
How could you say that to his face?

29:39.903 --> 29:42.530
That was then. He's good to me now!

30:07.555 --> 30:08.598
By then,

30:09.182 --> 30:11.392
the bloodstains had been
wiped away completely.

30:32.789 --> 30:34.040
I'm not sure.

30:34.541 --> 30:36.668
I can't remember every single guest.

30:37.168 --> 30:40.672
And even if I did, I can't just give out
our guests' personal information.

30:40.755 --> 30:43.424
And the car accident
has nothing to do with our hotel.

30:44.092 --> 30:46.511
If I may, why do you ask?

30:47.053 --> 30:48.304
What's this about?

30:48.805 --> 30:50.348
I see. Thank you.

31:09.450 --> 31:11.202
-Excuse me.
-Yes?

31:12.579 --> 31:14.122
-One moment, please.
-Yes?

31:14.205 --> 31:17.333
Have you seen this man among the guests?

31:17.876 --> 31:19.043
No, I haven't.

31:21.337 --> 31:22.964
Do you recognize this man?

31:24.465 --> 31:26.050
I've never seen him before.

31:29.888 --> 31:31.097
I don't know him.

31:35.977 --> 31:37.270
I'm not sure.

31:44.152 --> 31:45.778
Whoa, sorry.

31:46.446 --> 31:47.447
Apologies.

31:48.114 --> 31:50.658
You're not allowed in here.

31:53.036 --> 31:55.288
Sir? The exit is this way.

31:56.372 --> 31:57.373
I know that.

32:01.419 --> 32:02.253
Lee Kang?

32:05.340 --> 32:07.133
Is that you? Lee Kang?

32:08.801 --> 32:09.636
Jae-sik?

32:12.263 --> 32:13.306
Jae-sik!

32:13.389 --> 32:15.058
It was an incredible stroke of luck.

32:15.141 --> 32:16.017
How've you been?

32:16.100 --> 32:18.144
Had I not met Jae-sik at that moment,

32:18.728 --> 32:21.648
the truth would have stayed
buried in the dark forever.

32:28.446 --> 32:29.572
I first met Jae-sik

32:30.573 --> 32:31.991
last summer.

32:37.497 --> 32:38.915
"Lee Kang."

32:39.791 --> 32:40.750
High school senior?

32:43.711 --> 32:46.756
Don't seniors usually spend the summer
studying at the academy?

32:47.632 --> 32:49.676
Yet you're wasting
your precious time working.

32:50.176 --> 32:51.678
What a tough life.

32:57.433 --> 32:59.185
What are you studying?

33:02.355 --> 33:03.564
The civil servant exam?

33:05.066 --> 33:06.067
"Oh Jae-sik."

33:06.859 --> 33:08.111
I'm just getting started.

33:09.988 --> 33:12.573
Actually, it's my third attempt
at starting. Fuck my life.

33:17.662 --> 33:20.164
Holy crap, Yeonseo University?
Brainy bastard, huh?

33:23.126 --> 33:24.961
What about you? The civil servant exam.

33:26.379 --> 33:27.213
Not yet.

33:28.089 --> 33:29.841
I'm not giving up. Don't write me off.

33:30.591 --> 33:33.344
Write you off? Never.
You're cool just as you are.

33:35.221 --> 33:36.055
Really?

33:37.265 --> 33:40.309
I mean, yeah.
Working at the hotel isn't so bad.

33:42.020 --> 33:44.981
What about that car accident?
What do you want to know?

33:45.481 --> 33:47.608
Well, it's a long story.

33:48.276 --> 33:51.487
It's strictly personal.
I kind of knew the woman who died.

33:52.405 --> 33:54.157
Is that right?

33:54.657 --> 33:55.700
You knew her?

33:56.284 --> 33:58.077
Yeah, I just feel bad for her.

33:58.911 --> 34:01.873
I'd like to know what happened
before the accident,

34:03.499 --> 34:05.084
but no one will tell me shit.

34:07.712 --> 34:08.713
I bet no one else…

34:10.423 --> 34:12.091
knows more about it than I do.

34:14.427 --> 34:15.261
Really?

34:17.555 --> 34:18.473
I

34:19.974 --> 34:21.559
even witnessed the accident.

34:23.436 --> 34:25.730
I was on my way home from work.

34:27.565 --> 34:29.358
Talk to me before you go!

34:30.151 --> 34:30.985
I'm not talking…

34:31.069 --> 34:34.739
I recognized them right away.

34:34.822 --> 34:35.823
Especially…

34:35.907 --> 34:36.741
Min-hui!

34:36.824 --> 34:37.825
…that man.

34:38.910 --> 34:40.620
What? You scared?

34:41.412 --> 34:44.040
Just wait and see the shit I pull.

34:52.507 --> 34:54.217
-Call an ambulance.
-Holy crap.

34:54.300 --> 34:56.385
-What the…
-Someone call an ambulance!

34:56.469 --> 34:57.929
-We need an ambulance.
-My God!

34:58.012 --> 34:59.889
-A car accident.
-She came out of nowhere!

34:59.972 --> 35:01.641
Yeah, all of a sudden.

35:05.394 --> 35:06.479
That man.

35:07.146 --> 35:07.980
Who was he?

35:09.107 --> 35:10.149
That man

35:10.775 --> 35:13.319
was a regular at our suite.

35:15.154 --> 35:17.657
"A regular at the hotel suite"?

35:20.535 --> 35:21.661
Kim Su-hun was?

35:24.330 --> 35:26.290
He came three or four times a month

35:27.041 --> 35:29.001
and always reserved that room.

35:29.085 --> 35:31.003
But the funny thing is,

35:31.587 --> 35:33.589
he would always order top-shelf wine

35:33.673 --> 35:36.050
with a side of cheap ice cream
through room service.

35:36.134 --> 35:39.387
Wait, cheap ice cream? Why?

35:39.470 --> 35:42.765
I wouldn't know.
I guess that's up to our imaginations.

35:45.977 --> 35:48.271
Hello, sir. Room service.

35:50.481 --> 35:51.732
Thank you, sir.

35:55.486 --> 35:57.572
The woman's outfit changed every time.

35:58.072 --> 36:01.617
A nurse costume one day.
A bunny, the next.

36:02.118 --> 36:04.996
And another day, a schoolgirl uniform.

36:05.079 --> 36:06.330
Yeah, Mr. Choi.

36:07.415 --> 36:08.499
Not at all.

36:09.458 --> 36:10.877
I'm on a trip.

36:12.211 --> 36:14.547
No, just me without my wife.

36:15.548 --> 36:17.049
No, I'm not writing.

36:17.884 --> 36:19.343
I don't have anything written.

36:20.094 --> 36:23.097
-The truth is, he's an author.
-Just needed some inspiration.

36:23.890 --> 36:26.142
He probably thought
someone like me wouldn't know.

36:27.351 --> 36:28.477
He's an author?

36:29.103 --> 36:30.313
Yeah.

36:43.201 --> 36:44.952
Man, how could an author…

36:45.661 --> 36:47.079
And he's married, you say?

36:48.289 --> 36:50.166
Bastards like him are the worst.

36:50.249 --> 36:53.085
They act respectable in public
but are sick pervs in private.

36:54.295 --> 36:58.382
So that's what he was doing that day too?
The day of the accident?

36:58.883 --> 36:59.800
No.

37:00.301 --> 37:01.344
That day was

37:02.178 --> 37:03.387
a little different.

37:03.971 --> 37:05.556
A bit unusual, you could say.

37:06.724 --> 37:07.934
Unusual?

37:08.434 --> 37:11.979
Yeah. The noises I heard that day
were a little different.

37:12.855 --> 37:14.815
I didn't mean to eavesdrop, but…

37:17.193 --> 37:18.527
What different noises?

37:20.154 --> 37:20.988
Well, you see…

37:24.033 --> 37:25.159
WIFE

37:30.581 --> 37:33.584
What I heard was…

37:34.877 --> 37:35.711
PARK HYEONG-JONG

37:35.795 --> 37:38.047
Why are you people doing this?

37:41.842 --> 37:43.135
Professor Park, what is it?

37:43.219 --> 37:45.012
Mun-oh, where are you?

37:45.513 --> 37:47.139
Come on, why aren't you back yet?

37:47.223 --> 37:49.892
I'll be back soon. What is it?

37:49.976 --> 37:52.812
Mun-oh, guess who
is here with us right now?

37:53.312 --> 37:55.189
Do you know who we just bumped into?

37:55.940 --> 37:57.733
What are you talking about?

38:03.656 --> 38:04.657
Wait, who?

38:08.953 --> 38:10.621
Let's get one altogether.

38:11.163 --> 38:13.124
Three, two, one.

38:13.207 --> 38:14.041
There you are.

38:14.542 --> 38:15.751
Hey, Mun-oh.

38:16.752 --> 38:18.921
Fancy seeing you here, huh?

38:19.755 --> 38:20.798
How have you been?

38:21.590 --> 38:22.425
Why are you here?

38:22.508 --> 38:24.010
A surprise, isn't it?

38:24.510 --> 38:28.306
I spotted him on his way home
from a meeting with a publishing house

38:28.389 --> 38:30.308
and asked him to join.

38:30.391 --> 38:31.809
A publishing house?

38:33.311 --> 38:36.814
What took you so long in the restroom?
What were you doing?

38:36.897 --> 38:38.816
You didn't even answer my call.

38:39.900 --> 38:41.193
It wasn't that long.

38:41.277 --> 38:44.322
Anyway, I hope
I'm not interrupting your fun.

38:44.405 --> 38:45.239
Not at all.

38:45.323 --> 38:48.743
You're not interrupting at all.
I'm so excited right now.

38:48.826 --> 38:50.995
Meeting you has been
the highlight of the day.

38:51.078 --> 38:51.954
Absolutely.

38:52.038 --> 38:54.957
It's always an honor
to be in your company.

38:55.458 --> 38:59.378
He's talked about you a lot
since that lecture.

38:59.462 --> 39:04.133
He's been bragging to everyone
about the pleasure of meeting you.

39:05.301 --> 39:06.635
I see.

39:07.345 --> 39:10.097
This is the first I've heard
about the lecture.

39:12.016 --> 39:15.269
That's how this one is.
Always so reserved.

39:15.770 --> 39:18.731
I didn't even know
that you two were in college together.

39:19.231 --> 39:22.443
Is that right? Eun-joo and I
talked about you from time to time.

39:24.320 --> 39:25.446
Eun-joo?

39:26.530 --> 39:29.241
My wife went to the same school.
She's Mun-oh's junior.

39:34.747 --> 39:36.540
You two talked about me?

39:40.878 --> 39:42.755
And how is Eun-joo?

39:42.838 --> 39:44.632
Yeah, she's doing well.

39:44.715 --> 39:47.385
Actually, my second kid
is attending Yeonseo University.

39:47.468 --> 39:51.389
Turns out he's in your class.
So we talked about you sometimes.

39:53.599 --> 39:54.600
I see.

39:55.351 --> 39:56.685
That's news to me.

39:58.687 --> 40:01.941
What was he like back in university?

40:05.403 --> 40:07.363
Well, he was pretty reserved.

40:08.030 --> 40:12.118
Always sitting in the last row
of the lecture hall, like an observer.

40:12.201 --> 40:14.412
It was rather cunning.

40:14.954 --> 40:16.455
But that's also Mun-oh's charm.

40:16.539 --> 40:18.416
So you haven't changed a bit.

40:22.711 --> 40:26.048
And why did you meet with
the president of that publishing house?

40:26.924 --> 40:28.217
To discuss your next book?

40:28.300 --> 40:32.179
Not my next book. He's already
talking about the one that'll come after.

40:32.263 --> 40:35.057
But I need ideas for my next book
or the one after that.

40:35.975 --> 40:36.892
Speaking of,

40:37.893 --> 40:41.021
where do you usually get your ideas from?

40:43.816 --> 40:46.235
Where do you find new inspiration?

40:47.820 --> 40:49.071
Well, that's…

40:50.698 --> 40:53.284
What? Is it awkward to share?

40:54.910 --> 40:56.745
I'm just curious.

40:59.582 --> 41:01.041
Perhaps you

41:02.460 --> 41:05.671
travel to new places

41:06.589 --> 41:07.506
or…

41:10.509 --> 41:11.886
meet someone new

41:11.969 --> 41:14.555
and experience a thrilling deviation
from everyday life.

41:18.642 --> 41:21.020
I wouldn't call it
a deviation from my everyday life,

41:22.563 --> 41:25.232
but I do travel a lot. Why do you ask?

41:28.027 --> 41:29.111
The truth is,

41:29.653 --> 41:33.365
he's asking
because he's genuinely curious.

41:34.241 --> 41:37.495
He's been in a slump for a long time
since writing his first novel.

41:38.120 --> 41:39.538
So he's just curious

41:39.622 --> 41:42.041
how you do it.

41:43.292 --> 41:44.126
Is that so?

41:46.879 --> 41:48.214
Why the hell?

41:48.797 --> 41:50.132
Why the hell?

41:50.216 --> 41:51.884
Why did you say that crap, huh?

41:51.967 --> 41:56.013
Why would you say that crap about me
being in a slump in front of that bastard?

41:56.096 --> 41:58.057
And why didn't you tell me?

41:58.140 --> 42:00.809
Why did you hide the fact
that you went to school with him?

42:00.893 --> 42:01.727
What?

42:01.810 --> 42:05.189
Did you not want to even say his name
after he stole the girl you liked?

42:05.272 --> 42:07.775
-What did you say?
-That's her name, isn't it?

42:08.442 --> 42:10.611
Ahn Eun-joo, Kim Su-hun's wife!

42:11.445 --> 42:13.781
Who is she? Who even is she to you?

42:13.864 --> 42:16.992
You said it was all in the past.
What, still got feelings for her?

42:17.076 --> 42:19.703
Why do you keep hiding things from me?
I hate that!

42:19.787 --> 42:21.705
Hiding what? It's not like that.

42:22.957 --> 42:25.584
Or do you really have
an inferiority complex toward him?

42:26.585 --> 42:28.003
Is that why you didn't tell me?

42:28.087 --> 42:29.838
Are you done?

42:32.424 --> 42:35.970
Do you know what a son of a bitch
that bastard Kim Su-hun is?

42:43.852 --> 42:46.855
How am I supposed to know
if you don't tell me?

43:22.182 --> 43:24.143
It was an unusual day.

43:24.643 --> 43:27.229
The noises I heard that day
were a little different.

43:27.313 --> 43:29.940
How? What different noises?

43:31.442 --> 43:32.943
-Let go!
-Cut it out!

43:33.027 --> 43:35.195
Should I call your family?
Want me to call?

43:35.279 --> 43:38.407
Are you threatening me?
Keep testing me like this, and you'll pay!

43:38.490 --> 43:42.077
What? I'll pay?
And how exactly will you make me pay?

43:42.578 --> 43:44.538
Fine, you son of a bitch!

43:44.622 --> 43:46.165
Do whatever you want!

43:46.248 --> 43:48.709
I'll expose you for who you really are!

43:48.792 --> 43:49.960
I even have proof!

43:50.044 --> 43:52.379
-So they were fighting?
-I have proof right here!

43:52.463 --> 43:55.257
No, not so much fighting.

43:55.758 --> 43:58.469
More like hurling threats at each other.

43:58.969 --> 43:59.970
Threats?

44:01.430 --> 44:04.642
And what was it like
when you went into the room?

44:05.726 --> 44:07.978
He told me to leave the tray
by the door that day.

44:10.564 --> 44:12.399
I wonder what threats she made.

44:13.359 --> 44:15.277
And what was the proof she mentioned?

44:16.820 --> 44:19.448
Hello? Yes, I'll head back right away.

44:19.531 --> 44:20.532
Okay.

44:22.743 --> 44:24.703
-I should get back.
-Sure, Jae-sik.

44:25.412 --> 44:28.916
-Sorry I kept you for so long.
-No, this was fun. It was nice seeing you.

44:29.416 --> 44:30.542
-See you soon.
-Yeah.

44:30.626 --> 44:32.836
Come visit me. I'll be here, okay?

44:32.920 --> 44:33.879
See you.

44:36.340 --> 44:37.508
Right, yesterday.

44:38.300 --> 44:40.803
A guy about your age
came to the hotel yesterday.

44:41.345 --> 44:42.179
What?

44:42.262 --> 44:45.557
He asked if anything had happened
before the accident. Just like you.

44:48.644 --> 44:49.603
Really?

44:50.437 --> 44:51.271
Who was he?

44:52.106 --> 44:52.940
I don't know.

44:53.440 --> 44:56.193
But he asked me
something strange at the end.

44:57.903 --> 44:59.697
If it was really a car accident,

45:01.031 --> 45:03.033
or if it could have been a murder.

45:04.535 --> 45:06.120
-A murder?
-Yeah.

45:06.787 --> 45:08.580
It threw me off at first too.

45:08.664 --> 45:10.833
I witnessed the accident myself,
after all.

45:11.542 --> 45:16.797
But I thought hard about it after he left,
and something felt off.

45:17.965 --> 45:18.966
Don't you think?

45:19.049 --> 45:21.301
He wouldn't have known
the two of them fought.

45:21.885 --> 45:23.387
I didn't tell him either.

45:24.138 --> 45:27.933
So why did he suddenly bring up
the possibility of murder?

45:28.809 --> 45:30.018
What does he know?

45:30.769 --> 45:32.020
What does he suspect?

45:40.738 --> 45:41.905
Murder?

46:04.636 --> 46:07.097
Did you think this would be enough
to get rid of me?

46:08.599 --> 46:10.309
You crazy bitch!

46:20.068 --> 46:21.445
-Let go!
-Cut it out!

46:21.528 --> 46:23.697
Should I call your family?
Want me to call?

46:23.781 --> 46:27.034
Are you threatening me?
Keep testing me like this, and you'll pay!

46:27.117 --> 46:30.621
What? I'll pay?
And how exactly will you make me pay?

46:31.121 --> 46:33.081
Fine, you son of a bitch!

46:33.165 --> 46:34.500
Do whatever you want!

46:34.583 --> 46:37.002
I'll expose you for who you really are!

46:37.085 --> 46:39.671
I even have proof! I have proof right--

47:37.896 --> 47:39.273
Kim Su-hun.

47:41.942 --> 47:43.569
What have you…

47:45.821 --> 47:47.531
What did you do?

47:49.908 --> 47:51.785
What have you done?

48:00.836 --> 48:01.753
Hurry.

48:07.259 --> 48:08.093
Hey, Lee Kang!

48:08.844 --> 48:10.637
Find that young man.

48:11.263 --> 48:13.432
Mr. Heo? What time is--

48:14.266 --> 48:16.894
No, we need to know who that guy is!

48:16.977 --> 48:19.688
The young man who brought up
the possibility of murder.

48:20.689 --> 48:23.400
Go back to the hotel tomorrow
and try to find out who he is.

48:23.901 --> 48:27.154
Check all the security footage
if you have to. Then we're good.

48:28.822 --> 48:31.408
Then we'll know what that proof is.

48:31.909 --> 48:34.036
Mr. Heo, please calm down.

48:34.786 --> 48:36.955
You told me not to get
all worked up, remember?

48:37.539 --> 48:41.126
I was going to tell you tomorrow anyway…

48:43.253 --> 48:45.213
but I think I know who he is.

48:45.964 --> 48:46.924
What did you say?

50:20.225 --> 50:21.059
Sis?

50:27.149 --> 50:28.233
Dad…

50:33.405 --> 50:34.948
killed someone.

50:44.374 --> 50:45.667
I said Dad…

50:50.797 --> 50:52.466
killed someone.

51:01.767 --> 51:04.770
NOTES FROM THE LAST ROW

53:30.874 --> 53:35.879
Subtitle translation by: Jimin Choi
